<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's NYBB downgrades OTP.</title>
<headline>Hungary's NYBB downgrades OTP.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian brokerage firm New York Broker Budapest (NYBB) downgraded shares in OTP Bank to short-term &quot;sell&quot; from &quot;speculative buy&quot; and to long-term &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot;, on technical grounds.</p>
<p>NYBB assigned its previous recommendations to OTP shares on July 1.</p>
<p>&quot;The company's fundamentals have not changed since our recent recommendation on July 1...and the short-term sell recommendation is based on technical factors,&quot; analyst Gabriella Bor said in a research.</p>
<p>The analyst said NYBB expected an around 10 percent downward correction in OTP's price as it had risen more than 40 percent in one month.</p>
<p>-- Emese Bartha, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
